Identifiers are interned by service-name string:

- `_util.serviceIds` is a `Map<string, ServiceIdentifier<any>>`.
- `createDecorator` returns the cached identifier when present.
- Otherwise it creates the decorator function, assigns its string representation, caches it, and returns it. Thus equal service IDs share function identity. [instantiation.ts:12]({REPO_ROOT}/target/benchmarks/agent-navigation/final-2d6319d/r03-huge-vscode-plain/huge-vscode/src/vs/platform/instantiation/common/instantiation.ts:12) [instantiation.ts:109]({REPO_ROOT}/target/benchmarks/agent-navigation/final-2d6319d/r03-huge-vscode-plain/huge-vscode/src/vs/platform/instantiation/common/instantiation.ts:109)

The identifier function is also the parameter decorator. It requires the three decorator arguments and records `{ id, index }` on the target constructor through `storeServiceDependency`. The `$di$target` check ensures dependencies are appended only to metadata owned by that exact constructor; otherwise a fresh dependency array is created, avoiding mutation of inherited constructor metadata. [instantiation.ts:97]({REPO_ROOT}/target/benchmarks/agent-navigation/final-2d6319d/r03-huge-vscode-plain/huge-vscode/src/vs/platform/instantiation/common/instantiation.ts:97) [instantiation.ts:115]({REPO_ROOT}/target/benchmarks/agent-navigation/final-2d6319d/r03-huge-vscode-plain/huge-vscode/src/vs/platform/instantiation/common/instantiation.ts:115)

